{"title":"2024 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.1_(less_words)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.1 (less words)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(solution_1.1_with_graphing)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (solution 1.1 with graphing)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_(🚀_3_min_solve_🚀)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 (🚀 3 min solve 🚀)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_-_MaffyTaffy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 - MaffyTaffy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/0/800e523726ea86fd47d13302e6a768182e0cc4b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le\\theta\\le2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"89\" height=\"17\" /> satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/4/5444c7df391eb7689156f53a094bcb3b8b332a38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(\\sin(3\\theta))+\\log(\\cos(2\\theta))=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"244\" height=\"20\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/b/22b4eb6695e0e6b215583036498ed475b421f52f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }0 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }1 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }2 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }3 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }4 \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"353\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that this is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/a/9eabe50683ce5c4940f396b56dccd5f35d7372c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(3\\theta)\\cos(2\\theta)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"149\" height=\"20\" />, which is clearly only possible when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/8/f28dbc574484cb39640ab77a3448c28fc261e39e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(3\\theta)=\\cos(2\\theta)=\\pm1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"185\" height=\"20\" />. (If either one is between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, the other one must be greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> to offset the product, which is impossible for sine and cosine.) They cannot be both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> since we cannot take logarithms of negative numbers, so they are both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/7/1178af8fcc5f3f3acb9f151f7dcc2c4eefe88fd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/4/f34abb1905779a6fa2c98b8994448b09bd6a213e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\theta$\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/a/ceab18bb2a116d32000ff852501ef8715e6e5de1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac\\pi2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"17\" height=\"34\" /> more than a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/709acef3551b886e6754de72d59a88f00660f0d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/2/08221292fc5357dd032d4c088bd58915c3707f08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\theta$\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/709acef3551b886e6754de72d59a88f00660f0d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/6/4a69d2fd78c2b0bcd77b4976136f8286e8507e22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac\\pi6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"17\" height=\"34\" /> more than a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/5/1658dd7cb12f0c59c456920a1d36b04122cf31f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac23\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"26\" height=\"38\" /> and also a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />. However, a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/5/1658dd7cb12f0c59c456920a1d36b04122cf31f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac23\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"26\" height=\"38\" /> will always have a denominator of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and never <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />; it can thus never add with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/6/4a69d2fd78c2b0bcd77b4976136f8286e8507e22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac\\pi6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"17\" height=\"34\" /> to form an integral multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />. Thus, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/e/f1ea1f26eedb2d601fdd27e52e6dc0e5f4b4be7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"28\" /> solutions. \n</p><p>~Technodoggo\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1.1_.28less_words.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.1_(less_words)\">Solution 1.1 (less words)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.1 (less words)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/1/5413a0069a1c0b7e208f7568805bd39a5ff7c6fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log(\\sin(3\\theta))+\\log(\\cos(2\\theta))=0\\]\" width=\"241\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/d/f9db4feece7bb472f0ffed2cc65c238ecb1ba9d4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log(\\sin(3\\theta)\\cos(2\\theta))=0\\]\" width=\"184\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/e/2bed159f05bb9ecefff32b30073069a3b5fdb839.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin(3\\theta)\\cos(2\\theta)=1\\]\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/4/db4ed4fa0c7fe29c7a40f4115de83a742c585638.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Since } -1\\le \\sin(x),\\cos(x)\\le 1 \\Rightarrow \\sin(3\\theta)=\\cos(2\\theta)= \\pm1\\]\" width=\"445\" height=\"18\" />\nBUT note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a67c00939391484c6477561bd3fdf4612c934e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log(-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" /> is not real\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/a/1fa9cbde5db4d085b557213f9ce58a6199efa814.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Rightarrow \\sin(3\\theta)=\\cos(2\\theta)= 1\\]\" width=\"190\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3ba11370c8c85671049db5c7ec6aa915d5736e47.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3\\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+2\\pi n; \\space 2\\theta=2\\pi m \\space   (m,n \\in \\mathbb{Z})\\]\" width=\"278\" height=\"32\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/4/b84f1ec0578bc52c1d81e6ebc1e56b8274779a2c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{6}+\\frac{2\\pi n}{3}; \\space \\theta=\\pi m\\]\" width=\"173\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/e/42ebae291ec5bd000b0092d3f6d02aea38fa4861.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Rightarrow \\theta\\text { has no solution}\\]\" width=\"147\" height=\"13\" />\nGiving us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/b/f1b1d37ab44876bad45ea5bd533853b15e8f117f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{(A) 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"52\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Minor edits by evanhliu2009\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/b/39b6d90648a764909d483fcb7b3f68b6f53d7022.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(\\theta)=\\log(\\sin(3\\theta))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"152\" height=\"20\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/a/d0ac1ae0cb2b8ec8aba0add7f7357ceed837e95e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(\\theta)=\\log(\\cos(2\\theta))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"153\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/e/efe0a9c4bcd4d9675264991f3f49b845bac8d370.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1\\leq\\sin(3\\theta),\\cos(2\\theta)\\leq1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"202\" height=\"20\" />. Because the logarithm of a nonpositive number is not real, the functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> only exist when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/e/bfed0f035d7ee7327eae07ccc7a08ea603a0182b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(3\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/7/b77a839c66d7d5400e795517938dee088f6a3bb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(2\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" /> are positive, respectively. Furthermore, because the logarithm of any positive real number less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is negative, the only case where the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/3/0a378bcd66242ee0e583acb552e9d435dec89fde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f+g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" /> could equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/7/4f7b15818bc6dc82ff70c34a345d4fd81aa56fc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(\\theta)=g(\\theta)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" />, which only occurs when their respective sine and cosine expressions are both equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, we have these two equations, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are any integers:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\sin(3\\theta)=1 \\Rightarrow 3\\theta = \\frac\\pi2+2\\pi m &amp;\\Rightarrow \\theta = \\frac\\pi6+\\frac{2\\pi}3 m = \\frac{4m+1}6\\pi\\\\\n\\cos(2\\theta)=1 \\Rightarrow 2\\theta = 2\\pi n &amp;\\Rightarrow \\theta = \\pi n\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/d/81dc83c80f051dbfbffdc1236da9038357c4a203.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4m+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" /> is odd, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef83273691d41412d136de34fb111ee23f3629db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4m+1}6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"38\" /> is never an integer. Therefore, by the first equation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can never be an integer multiple of pi. Thus, because the second equation requires that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be an integer multiple of pi, these two equations cannot both be satisfied, and so there are no solutions to the given equation.\n</p><p>Thus, we choose answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/e/f1ea1f26eedb2d601fdd27e52e6dc0e5f4b4be7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28solution_1.1_with_graphing.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(solution_1.1_with_graphing)\">Solution 3 (solution 1.1 with graphing)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (solution 1.1 with graphing)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/1/5413a0069a1c0b7e208f7568805bd39a5ff7c6fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log(\\sin(3\\theta))+\\log(\\cos(2\\theta))=0\\]\" width=\"241\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/e/0ae81821ff841ec9c778e05782c174c77690be32.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log(\\sin(3\\theta))=-\\log(\\cos(2\\theta))=\\log(\\sec(2\\theta))\\]\" width=\"343\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/b/ffbbd2895702cb56a26fc083aacce7e652305597.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\therefore\\text{let } y=\\sin(3\\theta)=\\sec(2\\theta), y &gt; 0\\]\" width=\"259\" height=\"18\" />\nSketching the graphs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/1/b615a101ca78484ddd509a20faa3aaccc930d309.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\sin(3x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/c/9ec8447d07120b1ea6f1a67e10154d0ec4d4e81b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\sec(2x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/3/cf32406671fc9a01b1982019404e3f981a0f56b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />, we see there are no intersections.\n</p><p>Thus there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/e/f1ea1f26eedb2d601fdd27e52e6dc0e5f4b4be7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"28\" /> angles that work.\n</p><p>~oofitu\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_.28.F0.9F.9A.80_3_min_solve_.F0.9F.9A.80.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_(🚀_3_min_solve_🚀)\">Video Solution 1 (🚀 3 min solve 🚀)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 (🚀 3 min solve 🚀)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/QIilrdvsHtk\">https://youtu.be/QIilrdvsHtk</a>\n</p><p><i>~Education, the Study of Everything</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_-_MaffyTaffy\">Video Solution 2 - MaffyTaffy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 - MaffyTaffy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/SWr5fi96-lk\">https://youtu.be/SWr5fi96-lk</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A\" title=\"2024 AMC 12A\">2024 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2024 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2024 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2024 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem